  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The flavors",
   "texto": [
    "**맛** = taste. **맛이 어때요?** = how is he, what do you know?",
    "**매워요** (pica), **달아요** (is sweet), **짜요** (is salted).",
    "The temperature: **뜨거워요** (burning, very hot) and **차가워요** (cold).",
    "Recuerda que funcionan como verbos: 떡볶이가 **매워요** = el tteokbokki pica."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Too much.",
   "texto": [
    "**너무** = too much. **너무 매워요** = is too itchy.",
    "To deny, the front: **안 매워요** = does not itch.",
    "**괜찮아요** = okay, it's okay. It serves to calm down and also to say «No, thank you.»."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "A major change:",
   "texto": [
    "Some **ㅂ** finished adjectives change that consonant to **우** in front of a vowel-starting termination: **맵다 → 매워요**, **춥다 → 추워요**, **덥다 → 더워요**. It is an irregular pattern; that is why it is not said * Learn these common forms as a group."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "But, in the same sentence:",
   "texto": [
    "You know how to start a new sentence. To say «but» **dentro** in the same sentence, **-지만** is added to the root.",
    "맵다 (ser picante) → **맵지만** 맛있어요 = pica, pero está rico.",
    "비싸다 (ser caro) → **비싸지만** 맛있어요 = es caro, pero está rico."
   ]
